# A vunit bound to dut(rtl) instantiates the property follows and the
# sequence pair that dut's architecture declares (#66). Declared in
# another file, follows(a, b) is an HDL call to the parser, as
# (follows(a, b)) and {(pair(a, b))} are in any file, so their actuals
# are HDL expressions with no PSL Boolean around them. f1 and f2 fail
# at 75 ns (a = '1' at 65 ns, b = '0' at 75 ns) and c1 is hit at 35 ns
# (a = '1' at 25 ns, b = '1' at 35 ns). GHDL 6.0.0 runs no vunit item
# and NVC 1.23.0 cannot parse vunits, so the times are hand-checked.
gohard check --sim --tb tb
